# Manifest: Environment Variables for Python ETL Pipeline

## PostgreSQL Source Database
DB_HOST=10.8.66.137                 # PostgreSQL server IP/hostname
DB_PORT=5432                         # PostgreSQL port
DB_NAME=trading_system               # Database name
DB_USERNAME=postgres                 # Database user
DB_PASSWORD=n3u3d4!                  # Database password

## DuckDB Warehouse
WAREHOUSE_DB_PATH=./warehouse.duckdb # Path to DuckDB file (relative or absolute)

## Logging
LOG_LEVEL=INFO                       # DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR

## ETL Configuration
ETL_BATCH_SIZE=1000                  # Records to process per batch

## Usage

### Windows
```powershell
$env:DB_HOST = "10.8.66.137"
$env:DB_USERNAME = "postgres"
$env:DB_PASSWORD = "n3u3d4!"
$env:WAREHOUSE_DB_PATH = "C:\warehouse.duckdb"
python -m etl_pipeline.app
```

### Linux
```bash
export DB_HOST=10.8.66.137
export DB_USERNAME=postgres
export DB_PASSWORD=n3u3d4!
export WAREHOUSE_DB_PATH=/app/warehouse.duckdb
python3 -m etl_pipeline.app
```

### Docker
```bash
docker run -e DB_HOST=10.8.66.137 -e WAREHOUSE_DB_PATH=/data/warehouse.duckdb etl-pipeline
```
